---
import CateringCTA from '../components/sections/CateringCTA.astro';
import FeatureBlock from '../components/sections/FeatureBlock.astro';
import Hero from '../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import IngredientStrip from '../components/sections/IngredientStrip.astro';
import MenuCard from '../components/sections/MenuCard.astro';
import MenuGrid from '../components/sections/MenuGrid.astro';
import SectionOpener from '../components/sections/SectionOpener.astro';
import VisitBlock from '../components/sections/VisitBlock.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import site from '../content/site.json';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getMenu } from '../lib/menu';
import kulchaChole from '../assets/photos/kulcha-chole.jpg';
import kulchaPair from '../assets/photos/kulcha-pair.jpg';
import kulchaPlate from '../assets/photos/kulcha-plate.jpg';
import kulchaThali from '../assets/photos/kulcha-thali.jpg';
import dal from '../assets/photos/dal-makhani.jpg';
import bhurji from '../assets/photos/paneer-bhurji.jpg';
import saag from '../assets/photos/sarson-ka-saag.jpg';
import hero from '../assets/photos/tandoor-skewers.jpg';

const all = (await getMenu()).flatMap((c) => c.items);
// Featured dishes, matched by their POS name, each with its photograph. One renamed or removed in the POS is left out.
const featured = [
  { name: 'Aloo Kulcha', image: kulchaThali, alt: 'An Amritsari kulcha on a brass thali with chole, white butter and pickle' },
  { name: 'Amritsari Special Chole', image: kulchaPlate, alt: 'A tray of dark Amritsari chole beside a charred kulcha topped with butter' },
  { name: 'Dal Makhni', image: dal, alt: 'A ladle lifting creamy dal makhani from a dark bowl, swirled with cream' },
  { name: 'Sarson Ka Saag - Amritsari Special', image: saag, alt: 'Sarson ka saag topped with white butter, with makki di roti and radish' },
  { name: 'Paneer Bhurji', image: bhurji, alt: 'Paneer bhurji in a silver dish with red onion, coriander and lime' },
  { name: 'Tandoori Chicken Tikka', image: hero, alt: 'Chicken tikka and paneer skewers over glowing coals' },
]
  .map((f) => ({ ...f, dish: all.find((d) => d.name === f.name) }))
  .filter((f) => f.dish !== undefined);
---

<Layout
  home
  nav="overlay"
  title="Amritsar Junction | Punjabi Restaurant & Amritsari Kulcha"
  description="Punjabi restaurant in Sydney serving Amritsari kulcha, tandoori kebabs, dal makhani, butter chicken and chaat. Book a table, order online or plan catering."
  share={hero}
>
  <Hero
    image={hero}
    alt="Paneer, chicken and seekh kebab skewers smoking over hot coals"
    size="home"
    eyebrow="This week"
    title="Amritsar's food, brought to your table in Sydney"
    standfirst="Kulchas baked in the tandoor, black dal cooked slow, and the chaat of the Golden Temple's lanes. Pull up a chair."
    focus="50% 60%"
  >
    <Button slot="actions" href={site.bookingUrl}>Reserve a table</Button>
    <Button slot="actions" variant="secondary" href={site.orderUrl}>Order online</Button>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="signature-title">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionOpener
        eyebrow="The signature"
        title="The bread a whole city is named for"
        standfirst="In Amritsar, breakfast is a kulcha, crackling from the tandoor, with a bowl of dark chole and an onion on the side."
        align="center"
        id="signature-title"
      />
      <FeatureBlock
        image={kulchaPair}
        alt="Two golden Amritsari kulchas sprinkled with coriander seed and chilli on a hessian cloth"
        caption="Coriander seed and chilli, pressed into the dough before baking."
        side="right"
        eyebrow="Aloo kulcha"
        title="Pressed against the clay wall until it shatters"
        as="h3"
        arch
      >
        <p>Ask anyone from Amritsar what they miss and the answer comes fast: a proper kulcha. Not a soft naan, but a layered, stuffed bread pressed against the hot clay wall of the tandoor until the outside shatters and the inside steams.</p>
        <p>Ours is filled with spiced potato and onion, brushed with butter and finished with a knob of white makhan that melts into every crease. It comes the way it does at home, with tangy Amritsari chole, tamarind chutney and pickled onion. Tear, scoop, repeat.</p>
        <Button slot="actions" variant="tertiary" href="/gallery#kulcha">Read the kulcha story</Button>
      </FeatureBlock>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section home-dishes" aria-labelledby="dishes-title">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionOpener
        eyebrow="From the menu"
        title="Six dishes to begin with"
        standfirst={`A short taste of the ${all.length} dishes on our menu, from street chaat to the tandoor.`}
        size="md"
        id="dishes-title"
      />
      <MenuGrid>
        {featured.map((f) => <MenuCard dish={f.dish!} image={f.image} alt={f.alt} />)}
      </MenuGrid>
      <div class="home-dishes__more">
        <Button variant="tertiary" href="/menu">See the full menu</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <IngredientStrip image={saag} focus="50% 55%" />

  <VisitBlock />

  <CateringCTA
    image={kulchaChole}
    alt="A stack of tandoor-baked kulchas on a plate with a bowl of chole behind"
    caption="Kulchas and chole, a favourite for morning functions."
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  .home-dishes__more { display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-top: var(--space-7); }
</style>
